// Generated from Tribute's chapters 935-990 (the Crimson Tide crossover, from Tribute's side): title, place, who is in the scene and the chapter text. Text is verbatim.
window.TRIBUTE_CHRONICLE = [{"n":935,"title":"The Ship From Another World","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Dragonvale Harbour","who":"Jade, Devon, San and Joel","text":"One week had passed since the visitors from another world had departed. Lunareth had returned to its usual rhythm, until another unfamiliar vessel was sighted approaching Dragonvale Harbour. Jade: \"A quiet day at the harbour... It's nice to have a proper rest for once.\" Devon: \"Indeed. No reports, no summons, no unexpected incidents... Just a normal day like a Sunday.\" \"Princess Jade! Forgive the interruption, but another unfamiliar vessel has been sighted approaching the harbour.\" Jade: \"Another one?\" Devon: \"It seems our quiet day won't last after all. How large is it?\" \"Quite large, Your Highness. Larger than a merchant ship. Its design is unlike any vessel from our records.\" From beyond the familiar seas, another vessel had found its way to Lunareth: a great ship with a crimson dragon on its sails. Aboard the ship: \"This isn't Fair Tide. The architecture, the harbour... this world is completely different.\" \"And those mountains... Beautiful, though.\" \"We should make contact first before deciding what to do next.\""},
{"n":936,"title":"Two Worlds, One Conversation","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Dragonvale Harbour","who":"Jade, Devon, San, Joel and Soel","text":"At Dragonvale Harbour, Princess Jade and Devon were introduced to the visitors: Captain San and First Mate Joel of the Crimson Tide. San: \"Greetings. I'm San, captain of the Crimson Tide. And this is Joel, my first mate.\" Joel: \"A pleasure to meet you both.\" Jade: \"I'm Jade Gold of the Imperial Guard.\" Devon: \"I'm Devon Chadstone of the Imperial House.\" Jade: \"And this little one...?\" San: \"Soel. Our familiar. He travels with us everywhere.\" Joel: \"Fair Tide is a settlement we built after being displaced by a storm. It's home to people from many places and times.\" San: \"We were on an expedition when a strange sea brought us here. It seems fate has led us to another familiar world once again.\" Jade: \"It is remarkable... Our world, too, has received visitors from elsewhere over the years. Some encounters were brief, others left a lasting impact.\" Devon: \"I agree. Different seas, different homes... but perhaps the same questions for our people and our worlds.\" Jade: \"Would you join us for refreshments? It would be a good chance to talk more comfortably.\" San: \"We would be delighted. There is much we would like to learn and share with you.\" And so the two groups left the harbour together, seeking a quieter place to continue their conversation."},
{"n":937,"title":"Beyond the Familiar Sea","part":1,"loc":"🍵 A teahouse overlooking Dragonvale Harbour","who":"Jade, Devon, San and Joel","text":"Later, Jade and Devon brought San and Joel to a quiet teahouse overlooking Dragonvale Harbour. San: \"Fair Tide began with people displaced by a storm. Different backgrounds, different worlds, but we built a home together.\" Joel: \"A place where people can live, work, and belong.\" Devon: \"That reminds me of Dragonvale. People from many lands, different cultures, yet one home.\" Jade: \"Dragonvale has always been a place of trade and exchange. Different people and ideas can be challenging, but they make us stronger.\" Joel: \"Whether it's an empire or a settlement, people still have the same worries, hopes, and stubborn problems.\" San: \"And protecting those people is what matters most.\" Devon: \"Your ship is impressive. Its craftsmanship is unlike anything I've seen.\" San: \"The Horizon Engine has taken us farther than we once imagined.\" Devon: \"I'd very much like to learn more about it someday.\" Jade: \"I'd like to learn more about your world too: your Imperial Guard, your kingdom, and how you overcame Xima's curse.\" Joel: \"We're happy to share. And we'd like to hear more about Fair Tide and Veyren.\" Devon: \"Perhaps our meeting isn't a coincidence.\" Jade: \"Then let's keep this connection. For now, as friends.\" San: \"And perhaps, in time, as allies between our worlds.\" A new friendship had formed across different seas, and perhaps the first step toward a much larger journey. The worlds had met once, and what came next might change them both."},
{"n":938,"title":"The Weight of a Guardian","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Dragonvale Harbour and market","who":"Jade, San and Joy","text":"The morning after their gathering, Jade met San again at Dragonvale Harbour. This time San introduced her to another member of the Crimson Tide: Joy, the Warden of Fair Tide and Joel's older sister. Joy: \"Jade Gold, Imperial Guard of Lunareth.\" San: \"I thought you two might have a few things in common. Nothing dangerous. For once.\" Jade: \"Your guards seem to know the people here.\" Joy: \"They should. Protecting a city means knowing more than its walls. That's how I see Fair Tide, and why I thought you two should meet.\" Jade: \"You're rather well known.\" Joy: \"That comes with the work. Sometimes it's helpful. Sometimes it means I can't buy anything without someone asking a question.\" Jade: \"That sounds familiar.\" Later, a sudden commotion rose in the market when a delivery cart slipped on a slope, its cargo tumbling toward the crowd. Jade: \"Move! It's coming this way!\" Joy: \"I'll secure the rest!\" Afterwards: \"Everyone all right?\" \"A few bruises, I think. Nothing serious. The cart could use some attention, though.\" Joy: \"You acted like someone who's spent years keeping people safe.\" Jade: \"A Warden doesn't get to ignore trouble simply because it's inconvenient.\" \"Neither does an Imperial Guard.\" Jade: \"Different worlds. Different titles. But the responsibility feels much the same.\" Joy: \"A title means little if the people carrying it forget who they're protecting. And sometimes the people doing the protecting need someone who understands them.\" \"I think we're going to get along.\" \"I think so too.\" One wore the title of Imperial Guard, the other carried the responsibility of a Warden: across two worlds, they had discovered a familiar calling."},
{"n":939,"title":"Those Who Stand Beside Us","part":1,"loc":"⚓ The Crimson Tide, at Dragonvale Harbour","who":"Devon, Joel, Jade, San and Joy","text":"The next day Devon visited the Crimson Tide. While Jade, San and Joy explored Dragonvale, Devon and Joel found time for a quieter conversation, one built on a shared sense of duty, responsibility and reliability. Devon: \"San's gone into the city with Jade and Joy?\" Joel: \"Apparently, they've found plenty to talk about. Jade rarely runs out of questions when she meets someone interesting.\" \"Neither does San. Would you mind showing me around?\" \"Not at all. Welcome aboard.\" Joel: \"Everyone seems to know their responsibilities. A ship only functions when people can rely on one another.\" Devon: \"And when something goes wrong?\" \"Then we deal with it together.\" Devon: \"People often remember the person who gives the orders... not always the ones making sure those orders can actually be carried out.\" Joel: \"You sound like you've had some experience with that.\" Devon: \"Enough.\" Later, a crew member reported that a supply crate had been damaged during unloading. Joel and Devon inspected it together, quickly identifying the issue and working with the crew to secure the contents. \"If you lift it from that side, the base may give way.\" \"You're right. We'll support it underneath first.\" \"Good eye. You would have noticed eventually.\" \"Probably. But eventually isn't always soon enough.\" Devon: \"San trusts you. And Jade trusts you.\" Joel: \"She does. That's not something either of us should take lightly.\" Devon: \"Trust is easy to promise. Harder to deserve.\" Joel: \"And something you have to keep earning.\" \"Sometimes loyalty means disagreeing.\" \"That sounds remarkably familiar.\" \"I had a feeling it might.\" When Jade, San and Joy returned from the city as the afternoon light began to fade: \"It seems we weren't the only ones making friends.\" Guardians did not always stand at the front: sometimes they stood beside those who led, keeping promises that no one else could see. Across two worlds, five people had begun to recognise something familiar in one another."},
{"n":940,"title":"A Shared Purpose","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Dragonvale Harbour","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, San, Joel and Joy","text":"Several days after the Crimson Tide's arrival in Dragonvale, Jade and Devon reunited with the rest of their travelling party: Sky, Levi and Sally. Though their great journey had ended, the bond between the five had never faded. \"It's good to have everyone together again.\" \"It has been a while since we could say that.\" \"So, this is the famous Crimson Tide? I've been hearing plenty about them.\" Jade: \"Not just the captain. San, her First Mate Joel, and Joy, the Warden of Fair Tide. Joy is Joel's older sister, which explains the similar names.\" Sally: \"So they travel with family too. That sounds like our kind of people.\" Devon: \"Then it's time for a proper introduction. They've already learned the basics about us. Let's see how they receive the rest of the Canon Five.\" Later, at Dragonvale Harbour, Jade introduced her companions to the Crimson Tide's captain and crew. \"Welcome to the Crimson Tide.\" \"Good to meet you all.\" \"Any friends of Jade's are welcome.\" Sky: \"You must encounter many unusual illnesses on your journeys. How do you manage healing aboard?\" \"We have our own healers, and friends in Fair Tide who help us when needed.\" Levi: \"This ship is built for more than travel. You've planned well for both journey and defence.\" \"A ship needs to be ready for whatever we might face.\" Sally: \"Living aboard must require quite an amount of organization.\" \"It does. People, supplies, training... and making sure everyone still feels at home.\" As the afternoon wore on, the two groups shared stories of their journeys, their responsibilities, and the people they continue to protect. \"Different worlds, yet the same purpose in the end. People who protect, travel and keep their promise.\" \"Sounds like we've found kindred spirits.\" \"Then let's consider this the start of a lasting bond.\" Jade: \"Our great journey may have ended... Different lives, different duties... Yet when it truly matters, we will always be the Canon Five.\" The Canon Five remained Tribute's central travelling party, not only in battle, but in every new path yet to come."},
{"n":941,"title":"Different Paths, Familiar Hearts","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Dragonvale Harbour and Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, Maera and Liang","text":"The day after their initial gathering, the Canon Five spent more time with the Crimson Tide crew. Sky met the medical team, while Levi joined the scouts for a closer look at their operations. Maera, Head Midwife and Maternal Care Lead: \"Our approach combines herbal remedies, basic medicine, and restorative arcane methods when needed. We also focus on preventive care, keeping the crew healthy so they can keep travelling safely.\" Sky: \"It's a well-balanced system. I can see why your crew recovers quickly from long journeys. And you bring experiences we don't often encounter. It would be wonderful to learn from you as well.\" Levi: \"Your scout network is impressive. You cover sea routes, coastlines and inland terrain.\" Liang, Scout and Pathfinder: \"We rely on layered routes: regular scouting, local contacts and early warnings. It gives the crew time to prepare and adapt.\" Levi: \"That's the kind of system I'd like to study further. It could strengthen our own routes back home.\" Liang: \"Then let's compare what we've learned. Different lands, but the same goal: keeping our people safe.\" Later, the two groups met at a shared meal in Fair Tide, where they exchanged what they had learned. \"It's fascinating how much knowledge you all share so freely.\" \"Different skills, different experiences, yet they complement each other perfectly.\" \"Collaboration like this could help many people, on both sides.\" \"Different worlds, but the same priorities: people, safety, and a home to return.\" \"And it reminds me that no journey is ever travelled alone.\" \"I'm glad we did this. It feels like the start of something lasting.\" \"Different paths, but we understand each other in ways I didn't expect.\" \"New routes, new knowledge, new allies... That's a good way to keep moving.\" As evening fell over Dragonvale Harbour, new friendships had taken root, and plans for future collaboration had begun to form. \"Different paths... different worlds... yet familiar hearts. Our journey may have ended... but it seems new ones are already beginning. Together again, in a different world, with new friends beside us.\""},
{"n":942,"title":"The Canon Five, Together Again","part":1,"loc":"⚓ The Crimson Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, San, Joel, Joy, Dr AA, Iris and Sen","text":"That evening San invited Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally to a relaxed gathering aboard the Crimson Tide. After spending time with the crew and Fair Tide community, the Canon Five reunited once more, complete and together. \"It feels strange... yet so right to have everyone together again.\" \"The Canon Five, at last. It has been far too long.\" \"Different worlds, new friends... and somehow, it still feels familiar.\" \"A little louder, a little busier... but in a good way.\" Jade: \"Joy, thank you for looking after everyone during our visit. You make it feel like coming home.\" Joy: \"You're welcome. It's been a pleasure, especially seeing Jade's family, the Canon Five, reunited.\" Devon: \"I can see why you and San make such a good team. Your crew is like a family.\" Joel: \"Experience teaches you that a journey is easier when you have the right people beside you.\" Sky: \"Your medical approach is impressive, Dr. AA. You combine treatment with long-term care, even in a travelling crew.\" Dr AA: \"Likewise, Sky. Your knowledge and practical healing are remarkable. Perhaps we can exchange methods sometime.\" Levi: \"Your scout reports are incredibly detailed. The way you track terrain and movement is impressive.\" The scout: \"And your field instincts are sharp. We think alike, different but familiar approaches. Perhaps we can plan a joint expedition one day.\" Sally: \"I never expected to feel so at ease with another caregiver. You and your team truly look after everyone.\" Maera: \"It's the same for me. You have an amazing way of balancing family, duty and care. It's a privilege to learn from.\" Iris: \"We should train together sometime! Your field experience is solid, Sen. You handle both scouting and medical support so well.\" Sen: \"I'd like that. Your recon skills are on a different level, Iris. There's always more to learn.\" \"To new friends... To shared knowledge... To the bonds that cross worlds... To the people who stand with us... and to the Canon Five, still together, no matter where the journey leads.\" \"Different worlds. Familiar hearts. New horizons. And many more journeys ahead.\" Jade: \"Our journey against Xima's curse has ended, but the path ahead remains open. I'm glad we face it together, as friends, allies, and family.\" The Canon Five remained Tribute's central travelling party, Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, and with the support of the Crimson Tide and Fair Tide their story continued into new lands, new people and new possibilities."},
{"n":943,"title":"Researchers of Two Worlds","part":1,"loc":"📚 Dragonvale: the archive","who":"Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"A few days after the Canon Five reunited and settled into Dragonvale, Adrian arranged a meeting with three renowned researchers: Renn (Arcane Navigator / Arcane Trickster), Erynn (Arcane Scholar) and Mimi (Diviner). Fen: \"Thank you all for meeting us.\" Renn: \"It's an honour. I've heard much about the Canon Five.\" Erynn: \"The chance to compare our research across both worlds is invaluable.\" Mimi: \"I've been looking forward to this! There's so much we can learn from each other!\" Adrian: \"Perhaps we can begin with a broader comparison: the ancient systems of both worlds.\" Renn: \"A good starting point. The governing structures, flow of resources, and the roles they served share more than I expected.\" Mimi: \"And restoration structures too: how civilizations rebuilt after collapse, and what made their recovery last.\" Erynn: \"The route records are particularly fascinating. Several trade and expedition routes in both archives, though the details don't always align.\" Mimi: \"Which brings us to the historical inconsistencies! I've found at least a few events that are recorded differently, or not at all, across worlds.\" Renn: \"And then there are the magical networks: ley lines, mana conduits, and their interaction with natural systems. Comparing our models could reveal how they truly connect.\" As discussion continued, the five researchers laid out their findings side by side, piecing together new perspectives on both worlds. \"Different worlds, different records, approaches... Yet the more we compare, the clearer it becomes.\" \"The questions we ask may be different, but the goal is the same: to preserve knowledge, restore what was lost, and build a more stable future for both worlds.\" What began as a meeting of minds soon became a shared research venture, uniting the knowledge, curiosity and purpose of two worlds."},
{"n":944,"title":"Shared Archives","part":1,"loc":"📚 Dragonvale: the archive","who":"Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"The following days, Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi opened the archives of both worlds, laying out maps, records, blueprints and magic schematics side by side. \"Let's start with the ancient systems. The foundations are different, yet the underlying principles are strikingly similar.\" \"It shows the same cycle: creation, collapse, and restoration.\" \"Which brings us to the restoration structures. Your world's warding towers and ours' relay spires serve parallel functions.\" \"And when we compare the route records, the trade and expedition paths align more than we expected.\" \"There are gaps, though. Several key journals are missing, right where the historical inconsistencies begin.\" \"These inconsistencies aren't random. They suggest events were altered, accidentally or deliberately, in both worlds.\" \"Agreed. The timeline diverges in small ways at first, then widens. It's as if the same history was recorded twice... with different outcomes.\" \"Which makes the magical networks even more interesting! The flow patterns, node structures, and resonance signatures match across both worlds!\" \"A shared network... That would explain the cross-world phenomena we've seen. The two worlds may not be separate at all.\" \"Then our research has the same goal: to understand how the networks connect, why the records diverge, and what it will take to repair what was lost.\" \"Different worlds... different methods... but the same curiosity... and the same hope. Looks like we make a pretty good research team!\" As the sun set over Dragonvale, the five researchers agreed to combine their findings into a unified archive, a bridge of knowledge between the two worlds."},
{"n":945,"title":"Patterns Across Worlds","part":1,"loc":"📚 Dragonvale: the archive","who":"Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"With their findings in hand, Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi reconvened to look beyond individual records, seeking the patterns that connected the two worlds. \"We've compared the records, the structures, the routes and the gaps... Now let's look at the bigger picture. Not just what happened in each world, but how and why the patterns repeat.\" \"There are enough overlaps that they can't all be coincidence. The question is what connects them.\" 1. Ancient Systems: both worlds built large-scale systems to channel and stabilize energy. Different designs, but the same purpose. 2. Restoration Structures: the restoration methods also align: staged recovery, network recalibration, and gradual reactivation. 3. Route Records: they show similar anomalies: shifting passages, repeating landmarks, and routes that defy normal distance. 4. Historical Inconsistencies: the gaps in our histories occur around similar periods: major upheaval, reconstruction, and the loss of key knowledge. 5. Magical Networks: they follow comparable structures: nodal flow, resonance linkages, and stabilizing anchors. \"Put together, they form a pattern: periods of advancement, instability, loss, and renewal. A cycle that appears in both worlds... with similar triggers and outcomes. Which suggests a shared influence. Not necessarily a single origin, but a common mechanism or force. Perhaps it's a network larger than either world, something that interacts with both in cycles. Then our next step is to test the theory. If the patterns are real, we should be able to find traces of the next cycle forming.\" \"For the first time, it feels like we're not just filling gaps in history... but following a thread that runs through both worlds. Different peoples. Different histories. But the same questions, the same patterns, and perhaps... the same future to protect. Then let's keep going together. There's still much to uncover, and I'd rather do it with all of you than alone in either world.\" The patterns were only the beginning: with a shared theory now in reach, the five researchers prepared to put their findings to the test, on the sea, on the land, and perhaps in the spaces between both worlds."},
{"n":946,"title":"The Black Pearl","part":1,"loc":"📚 Dragonvale: the archive","who":"Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"With the alliance now formalised, the joint research team turned its attention to the Black Pearl. \"First, let's establish the basics: the Black Pearl is ancient, far older than any of our current kingdoms.\" \"The records and comparative analyses are consistent. Its origin predates our known historical periods by a vast margin.\" \"And its functions are clear: restoration and preservation. It doesn't merely heal or repair; it preserves and stabilises what should endure.\" \"More than that, our analysis shows it can interface with systems beyond Lunareth. The Pearl is not limited to a single world's framework.\" \"In short... the Black Pearl is an ancient relic with the proven ability to restore, preserve, and interact across systems beyond Lunareth.\" \"Next, Devon's dragon abilities. Our cross-reference of bloodline records, manifestation patterns, and arcane signatures confirms it clearly... Devon's dragon abilities come from his bloodline, not the Pearl. They are hereditary, passed down through his family line.\" \"The Pearl may resonate with certain systems, perhaps stabilising them, but it is not the source of his power.\" \"Which brings us to the final, and still unanswered, question: its original owner. Despite all our records, comparisons, and cross-system traces... we must conclude that the Pearl's true original owner remains unknown. For now, it stands as the greatest open question in our research.\" Current findings: 1. Devon's dragon abilities come from his bloodline, not the Pearl. 2. The Pearl is ancient. 3. It has restoration and preservation functions. 4. It can interact with systems beyond Lunareth. 5. Its true original owner remains unknown. This mystery will guide the next stage of the shared inquiry."},
{"n":947,"title":"The Black Pearl (II)","part":1,"loc":"📚 Dragonvale: the archive","who":"Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"With the first findings confirmed, the crossover team pressed deeper. \"The records agree on the origin. The Pearl is older than Lunareth's known eras.\" \"Its functions are broader than repair. Preservation. Stabilisation. Continuity. It does not belong to one world alone.\" \"Devon's abilities are hereditary. The Pearl is not their source.\" The bloodline comparison (dragon signature): Devon (subject), family records (bloodline) and the Black Pearl (signature): Devon and the family records match (hereditary); the Black Pearl does not (not the source). \"The Pearl may resonate with Devon's abilities, but it did not create them.\" \"Every path toward the original owner ended in an incomplete record\": a parchment, The Core Keeper, with a missing piece. \"We have no confirmed owner. Only traces.\" Ancient. Restorative. Cross-system. Owner unknown. Key findings (verified): Devon's abilities are hereditary; the Pearl is ancient; restoration and preservation are core functions; it can interact beyond Lunareth; its true original owner remains unknown. The evidence was strong enough to guide the next stage of the inquiry, but not strong enough to reveal who first held the Black Pearl."},
{"n":948,"title":"The Black Pearl (III)","part":1,"loc":"📚 Dragonvale: the archive","who":"Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"With the data cross-checked and further analysis complete, the Crossover Research Team reconvened to consolidate their findings on the Black Pearl. Renn: \"So, we can now confirm Devon's dragon abilities are hereditary, from his bloodline, not from the Pearl.\" Erynn: \"The Pearl is ancient, likely from a time long before Lunareth, predating the current eras of Lunareth and Dragonvale.\" Mimi: \"Its core functions are restoration and preservation. It can repair, stabilise, and maintain life, matter, and certain systems.\" Adrian, Prince-Consort of Tribute and Royal Scholar: \"The Pearl can also interact with systems beyond Lunareth, which explains its influence across nations, and possibly other worlds or realms.\" Fen, Queen of Dragonvale and Royal Scholar: \"However, one critical detail remains unresolved: its true original owner. We have no confirmed records, mark, or signature thus far.\" The Black Pearl, current findings: Devon's dragon abilities are hereditary (from his bloodline), not from the Pearl. The Pearl is ancient, predating Lunareth and the current eras. Core functions: restoration and preservation (healing, repair, stabilisation, maintenance). It can interact with systems beyond Lunareth (multi-world potential). Its true original owner is still unknown. Key questions ahead: Who was the Pearl's original owner? Are there more Pearls, or is this truly one of a kind? What other worlds or systems can it connect to? What risks come with a fuller activation? Can its restoration functions be expanded or refined? Renn: \"Then our next step is to expand the search: check Tribute's archives, Dragonvale's sealed records, and any cross-world references we can find.\" Erynn: \"I'll compile a list of correlated artefacts and past anomalies that might link to the Pearl's origin.\" Mimi: \"And I'll continue tracing its resonance. It still feels like it's connected to something, or someone, waiting to be found.\" Adrian: \"I'll coordinate with both kingdoms for access and support. If the Pearl can bridge worlds, we can't leave its study unfinished.\" Fen: \"Agreed. The Pearl is more than an artefact. It's a key, perhaps to forgotten history, lost knowledge, and a story that still hasn't reached its end.\" With their conclusions aligned, the team set the next phase in motion: a wider search across kingdoms, archives, and beyond, to uncover the true origin and purpose of the Black Pearl."},
{"n":949,"title":"An Ally, Not a Kingdom","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Aboard the Crimson Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Adrian, Fen, San, Joel and the Crimson Tide crew","text":"Following the shared research and growing trust, Lunareth and the Crimson Tide formalised a working alliance: not a union of kingdoms, but a partnership of purpose. \"Today, we formalise our alliance: shared knowledge, mutual support, and cooperation across our worlds. It gives us the strength to face future threats together, while still respecting each world's independence.\" \"The Crimson Tide isn't a kingdom... but you are an invaluable ally. And Lunareth has always believed that allies are built on trust, common goals, and people who keep their word.\" \"Then let's keep it simple: we stand with you, and you stand with us.\" \"Our goals align: safer seas, open exchange of knowledge, and support when it truly matters.\" \"We'll share what we can, lend a hand when needed, and be there when you call.\" \"And we will do the same. Different worlds, different paths... but the same purpose.\" The Alliance Agreement, Lunareth x Crimson Tide, Working Alliance: Knowledge and Research Exchange; Mutual Support (Personnel, Supplies, Expertise); Crisis Assistance (By Request); Cultural and Trade Cooperation; Respect for Sovereignty and Autonomy. \"This will also be recorded in Tribute's existing Ally Network, with the Crimson Tide added as an ally.\" \"No new travel system is needed. We'll use the existing network for coordination, exchange and support.\" \"It's good to be part of a crew that builds bridges, not walls.\" The Tribute Ally Network now lists Dragonvale, Fair Tide, Lunareth and, new, the Crimson Tide. More than an agreement, it was a recognition that in a world with many paths, allies make the journey stronger. The Crimson Tide now stood beside Lunareth in Tribute's Ally Network: an ally in action, not a kingdom to be claimed."},
{"n":950,"title":"The Open Invitation","part":1,"loc":"⚓ Aboard the Crimson Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, San and Joel","text":"Following the alliance, the two groups gathered aboard the Crimson Tide, not for another agreement, but for an invitation. \"Now that the formalities are settled, there's something else we'd like to offer.\" \"Another agreement?\" \"Something much less complicated.\" \"Come aboard whenever you like. Spend time with us, explore with us, and even visit Fair Tide.\" \"You're inviting all of us?\" \"Of course. You've made us welcome here. We'd like to return the kindness.\" Devon: \"Our responsibilities remain here in Lunareth. And Dragonvale will always be our home.\" \"We're not asking you to leave it. Think of the Crimson Tide as a bridge. You can cross it and still have somewhere to return to.\" Sky: \"I'd certainly like to see how your healers work. There may be techniques we could share.\" Levi: \"And your scouts know routes beyond our maps.\" Sally: \"I'm more interested in what everyone does for entertainment.\" \"You should meet Mez.\" Beyond the unfamiliar seas lay Fair Tide, a settlement built by people who had once been strangers to their own world. \"It's not a kingdom. Just a place we've worked hard to make into a home.\" \"That sounds like somewhere worth visiting.\" Jade: \"Then let us be clear. We remain citizens of Lunareth, and our duties here come first.\" \"Naturally. An invitation shouldn't come with conditions.\" \"In that case... I'd be delighted.\" \"And if our scholars wish to continue their exchanges?\" \"They'll always find someone willing to talk research at Fair Tide.\" \"I have a feeling those conversations could last for days.\" They had not surrendered their homeland, their loyalties, or the lives they had built: they had simply discovered that home and possibility could exist on opposite sides of the same horizon. \"Then we'll see where this bridge takes us.\" \"Whenever you're ready.\""},
{"n":951,"title":"Guests of Fair Tide (I)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, San, Joel, Joy, Dr AA, Maera, Senedra, KW Liang, Iris, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"The harbour of Fair Tide was no longer unfamiliar to the visitors from Lunareth. They had come before, shared meals, exchanged knowledge and discovered friendships that crossed worlds. This time, they intended to stay a little longer. Jade: \"I have to admit, I missed this place.\" \"You missed the tavern.\" Levi: \"That too. I'm capable of appreciating several things at once.\" \"Some things never change.\" San: \"Welcome back! I hope you've brought clothes you don't mind getting dirty.\" Joel: \"You've been here before. You know how this place works.\" \"Since you're staying longer, perhaps you could help with a few things.\" \"What sort of things?\" \"Repairs, patrols, medical supplies, and a few problems nobody has managed to solve.\" \"That sounds more interesting than sitting around.\" \"I was just getting comfortable.\" San: \"You don't need to prove yourselves to anyone here. But if you want to help, we'll find something useful for each of us.\" \"That's why we came.\" \"Good. Because we don't have much use for ceremonial guests.\" Their skills, once shaped by Lunareth's dangers, found new purposes in Fair Tide. Dr AA: \"Your medical methods are different, but there's plenty we can learn from each other.\" Senedra and KW Liang: \"This route needs another lookout.\" Iris: \"Someone has been changing these delivery figures.\" Renn: \"You're back! We kept the records you wanted to compare.\" Erynn: \"Excellent, I brought additional copies from Lunareth.\" Mimi: \"Then perhaps we can finally resolve that discrepancy.\" \"Or discover three more.\" \"We didn't want to trouble the captain.\" \"You aren't troubling anyone. Tell us what happened.\" \"You really don't stop being an Imperial Guard.\" \"Some habits are worth keeping.\" \"I thought we were coming here to rest.\" \"You are resting.\" \"After an entire day of work?\" \"That's how Fair Tide welcomes people.\" Devon: \"We've travelled far beyond anything Lunareth once imagined.\" Jade: \"And somehow, this place is starting to feel familiar.\" \"We still have our lives at home.\" \"Of course. But there's room in those lives for another place.\" They remained citizens of Lunareth, with responsibilities and loved ones waiting across the worlds. Yet Fair Tide was becoming more than a destination: it was becoming somewhere they could belong."},
{"n":952,"title":"Guests of Fair Tide (II)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, Joy, Dr AA, Maera, Senedra, KW Liang, Iris, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"The Canon Five's return soon filled Fair Tide with familiar energy and a new round of projects, ideas and collaborations. With more time this stay, they threw themselves into the work, side by side with Fair Tide's crew and residents. \"It feels different.\" \"Familiar, doesn't it?\" \"We're no longer just visitors.\" \"We're part of the work now.\" Joy: \"Your help has already made a difference. The community is grateful, even if we keep adding new requests.\" Dr AA: \"Your treatment methods are practical and effective. And your knowledge from Lunareth gives us new options. It's a good exchange.\" Maera: \"These herbs from Lunareth are fascinating. They might work well with our current formulas.\" Senedra: \"This route needs another lookout, but it's manageable.\" KW Liang: \"I'll update the map and add a safer supply path.\" Iris: \"The discrepancy is real: someone has been redirecting supplies. I'll trace the records further. It might connect to a larger network.\" Devon: \"Your previous findings were right. This matches a similar record from Lunareth.\" Renn: \"Then it's not a coincidence. We may be looking at a shared origin.\" Erynn: \"If the energies are linked, it explains why the readings shift.\" Mimi: \"Which means both worlds may have more in common than we realised.\" \"I admit, I didn't expect to feel this settled.\" \"The work is challenging, but it's fulfilling.\" \"And the people make it easier.\" \"Fair Tide isn't perfect, but it's honest.\" \"And it has a way of turning strangers into friends.\" \"That's exactly what we hope for.\" Jade: \"I'm glad we came back.\" \"Me too. This place... it gives us something Lunareth never could.\" Their time in Fair Tide was no longer a brief visit, but a shared chapter of work, friendship and new possibilities. The world was wider than they had known, and so were the lives they could build."},
{"n":953,"title":"Shared Work, New Paths","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally, Joel, San, Joy, Dr AA, Maera, Senedra, KW Liang, Iris, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"With the guests settled in Fair Tide, work began in earnest, combining Lunareth's expertise with Fair Tide's resources and experience. It was more than a visit now: it was a true collaboration, with different skills and perspectives and the same goal, progress. Jade: \"Let's start by aligning our current projects.\" Devon: \"We can integrate the records from both sides.\" Sky: \"And test which methods work better under Fair Tide's conditions.\" Levi: \"Ranged support and field tests can be ours. We're used to adaptive operations.\" Sally: \"I'll help with analysis and coordination across both teams.\" Dr AA: \"Your team's medical logs are impressive. Combining them with our field data could improve long-term care for the crew.\" Maera: \"I'd like to explore some of Lunareth's herbal formulas. A few of them could support recovery and preventative care.\" Senedra and Liang: \"We've identified three routes for the next survey. One is safer, but longer. The other two are faster, with higher risks.\" Iris: \"I'll cross-check our findings with the existing maps and update the routes.\" Renn: \"The arcane signatures here are similar to Lunareth's second frontier.\" Erynn: \"Which means our frameworks might be compatible. This could open new research paths.\" Mimi: \"I can run a few divination readings to check for anomalies along the survey routes.\" Joel: \"Looks like we're all busy again. Feels familiar.\" San: \"Different people, but the same kind of chaos.\" Joy: \"A good kind of chaos. It means we're building something together.\" \"Projects, people, ideas... it feels less like work and more like a shared venture.\" \"Fair Tide really has a way of bringing people together.\" Jade: \"Lunareth still has its battles... but I'm glad we can work on this here.\" Devon: \"This is more than an alliance, Jade. It's a bridge: between our worlds, our people, and what comes next.\" New plans took shape, new bonds grew stronger, and a shared path began to unfold. The work ahead was still vast, but for the first time it didn't feel like two separate worlds: it felt like one journey with a wider horizon."},
{"n":954,"title":"New Circles (I)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, San, Joy and Joel","text":"The visitors from Lunareth had become familiar faces in Fair Tide. Now they began finding their place within the community: working, planning and solving problems together. Jade: \"The eastern walkway is still unsafe. If we're expecting more supplies next week, we should fix it now.\" Joy: \"Agreed. I've had similar reports from the harbour team. The supports are wearing out faster than expected.\" San: \"Then let's inspect it together. We can redirect the heavier deliveries for now and schedule proper reinforcements.\" Jade: \"We'll reinforce the main supports and widen the load path.\" Joy: \"I'll coordinate with the harbour team and get the materials ready.\" San: \"I'll have the scheduling updated and inform the supply crews.\" Devon: \"The current patrol route leaves the storage area unguarded during shift changes.\" Joel: \"Good catch. We can overlap the routes and cover it without adding more guards.\" \"It's good working with all of you. Different backgrounds, but we think similarly.\" \"That's probably why it feels so easy.\" \"Different worlds, different experiences... but the same goal: a safer, stronger Fair Tide.\" \"And it's only the beginning. I'm glad we're building these new circles together.\" They came from different worlds, carrying different histories and responsibilities. But here in Fair Tide, new circles of friendship had begun to form: not through titles or obligations, but through shared work, trust and purpose."},
{"n":955,"title":"New Circles (II)","part":2,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the infirmary","who":"Sky, Jenika, Maera, Eliz, Dr AA, Sister Wren, Senedra and Jovie","text":"As work in Fair Tide continued, new connections formed in the infirmary, where different worlds shared the same purpose: keeping people safe and healthy. Sky: \"Your herbal formulas are impressive, Jenika. We use something similar, but your method is more refined.\" Jenika: \"I'm glad it's useful. You have a good eye for adaptation, Sky.\" Maera: \"It's refreshing to compare our treatments. Different ingredients, but the goals are the same.\" Eliz: \"And it's nice having more hands in the infirmary. We can finally catch up on the backlog of checks!\" Dr AA: \"With the Tribute team here, we can expand the infirmary's care, not just for the crew, but for the whole settlement.\" Sister Wren: \"More people also means more responsibility. But it's a good problem to have.\" Senedra: \"I'll coordinate the field care supplies and recovery records.\" Jovie: \"And I'll assist with the daily treatments and follow-up checks.\" \"If we combine our knowledge: Lunareth's herbal records, Veyren's formulas, and Fair Tide's field experience... we could develop a shared medical protocol for long voyages and remote regions.\" \"That would be valuable for future expeditions.\" \"Exactly. A common framework means better care, wherever we go next.\" Jenika: \"It's remarkable how quickly we've found our rhythm. Different worlds, different training... but we all believe in the same thing: people's well-being.\" In the infirmary and beyond, a new circle of friendship had taken root, built on knowledge, care and a shared commitment to protect life."},
{"n":956,"title":"New Circles (III)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Levi, Sally, Mirelle, Jade, Devon, San, Joy, Joel, Iris, KW Liang and Sairen","text":"As the two groups settled further into Fair Tide, new circles of friendship continued to grow through shared information, trusted networks, and the quiet work that kept the settlement running smoothly. Levi: \"The supply routes are stable again. I've also confirmed new trade activity from the southern islands.\" Iris: \"I've cross-checked with our contacts. Nothing suspicious for now.\" KW Liang: \"Let's keep a closer watch on the new merchant group. It's not a threat, but they're more organised than they appear.\" Sally: \"News spreads fast in Fair Tide. I've already heard three different versions of the same thing.\" Sairen: \"Which is exactly why we verify it before sharing it further.\" Mirelle: \"Fair Tide is far more active than I expected. It's an excellent place to build connections, with the right balance.\" Jade: \"With the field intel and information networks in place, we'll have a clearer picture of what's happening across Fair Tide.\" San: \"It's good to see how quickly our teams are working together. Different skills, but the same purpose.\" Joy: \"And it's not just work either. They're already sharing meals, ideas, and a few laughs.\" Devon: \"Looks like we've gained more than allies here.\" Joel: \"A bigger crew, more friends... and probably more trouble in the future.\" From intelligence to diplomacy, from networks to community ties, new bonds were forming across Fair Tide. Different worlds, different paths, but a shared commitment to a safer home."},
{"n":957,"title":"New Circles (IV)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally and San","text":"After months of working, sharing knowledge, joining expeditions and being part of Fair Tide's daily life, a new chapter was finally within reach for the Canon Five. San, Captain and Council Liaison: \"For your continued contributions to Fair Tide, through research, healing, exploration, security and intelligence, the Council is pleased to grant the Canon Five permanent residency in Fair Tide. This residency recognises not just your work, but the trust, friendship and home you've built with our people.\" Jade (Imperial Guard, Expedition Leader): \"Fair Tide has given us more than alliances. It's given us a place to belong.\" Devon (Prince of Dragonvale, Strategist): \"A second home, then. It will certainly make future research and expeditions more convenient.\" Sky (Physician, Healer): \"I'm so glad. Fair Tide is full of good people, good food, and endless new things to learn.\" Levi (Ranger, Explorer): \"It's a smart move. This place is a valuable base, and honestly, it already feels like home.\" Sally (Information Specialist, Agent): \"A second home... That sounds nice. It makes future operations here much smoother too.\" \"To Fair Tide, our second home!\" \"To the people who made us feel welcome!\" \"To new expeditions and shared endeavours!\" \"To friendships across worlds!\" \"And to many more trouble-free days... hopefully!\" Residency does not replace their Lunareth citizenship. It grants the Canon Five the right to reside, work and operate in Fair Tide long-term. As the sun set over the harbour they found themselves not just as visitors or allies, but as part of Fair Tide's wider family, with new ties, new responsibilities and a home to return to."},
{"n":958,"title":"Second Home","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"With their permanent residency confirmed, the Canon Five began to settle more deeply into Fair Tide, not as visitors but as part of the community. Jade: \"It still feels a little surreal, to have a second home here now.\" Devon: \"It doesn't change where we're from, but it does mean we can build things here for the long term.\" Sky: \"More time for people, for learning, for healing... I couldn't ask for a better place.\" Levi: \"It's a good balance. Lunareth will always be home, but Fair Tide is home too.\" Sally: \"Two worlds, two homes, and a wider family now.\" Residency opened new opportunities: longer projects, shared research, continued expeditions and deeper community involvement. Devon: \"With a longer-term base, we can finally continue the draconic trade and cultural studies properly.\" Sky: \"And expand the infirmary's programmes too, especially the coastal health initiatives we discussed earlier.\" Levi: \"The residency also makes it easier to plan longer expeditions to the southern islands.\" Sally: \"And to keep the information networks running smoothly between Fair Tide, Lunareth and our other allies.\" Jade and San at the map table: \"Being here long-term lets us take on more responsibility, for the people, the harbour and what comes next.\" \"You've already made a real difference. Now, with roots here, we can plan further ahead, together.\" \"To Fair Tide, our second home!\" In the days that followed, routines settled into something new: familiar in their closeness, yet full of fresh possibilities. Two homes, shared purpose, and a wider world still waiting ahead."},
{"n":959,"title":"Roots in Fair Tide","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"Days turned into weeks, and the Canon Five began truly settling into life at Fair Tide: setting up homes, continuing their work and weaving themselves into the community. Jade: \"It feels good to have a place to return to, not just for work, but for life.\" Devon: \"Fair Tide has the resources, people and freedom to pursue projects we could only plan before.\" Sky: \"I've already started working with the infirmary on a longer-term health programme! There's so much we can do here.\" Levi: \"The trade routes, the expeditions, the new lands to explore... I'm looking forward to what comes next.\" Sally: \"And I've already expanded the information network here. Fair Tide is a good base: connected, active, and full of opportunities.\" Together they mapped out their next phase: research, trade, health initiatives, expeditions and joint operations across both worlds. \"Let's align our projects so they support both Fair Tide and our work elsewhere.\" \"Research, trade and health can all be integrated.\" \"And we'll keep the expeditions active; there's still so much out there.\" \"A wider network, shared intelligence and stronger coordination will make future work far more effective.\" \"To new beginnings at Fair Tide! To friends, allies and the people here! To the work ahead and all the challenges still to come! To two homes that make us stronger! And the stories we'll build from here on!\" The Canon Five were now permanent residents of Fair Tide, still holding their Lunareth citizenship, their work spanning both worlds. Under the evening sky they no longer felt like visitors: they had found a second home, a place for work, for friendship and for the next chapter of their journey."},
{"n":960,"title":"The Cold Spring","part":2,"loc":"♨️ Fair Tide: the Cold Spring","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally and San","text":"A few days after settling their residency, San suggested a simple outing, a visit to one of Fair Tide's natural springs near the hills. San: \"If you have time today, why don't we visit the Cold Spring? It's a favourite spot among the crew. It's a good place to unwind, especially after weeks of travel, meetings and settling in.\" Devon: \"A spring? I've heard about it, but haven't had the chance to go.\" Sky: \"A proper soak sounds perfect! My shoulders are still sore from the last expedition.\" Levi: \"Cold Spring... Is it very cold?\" Sally: \"From what I heard, it's refreshing rather than freezing. I'm curious now.\" San: \"It's cool and clear, with minerals that are said to be good for relaxation and general wellness. Nothing complicated, just a nice break.\" \"This is wonderful... It's been a while since I've felt this relaxed.\" \"The water is cooler than I expected, but it's so refreshing!\" \"It really soothes the aches. No wonder the crew likes it.\" \"It's pleasant... I can see why this place is popular.\" San: \"It's one of my favourite places here. Whenever things get hectic, a visit to the spring always helps me reset.\" \"Little moments like this make Fair Tide feel even more like home.\" \"Soak, good food and good company: not a bad way to live.\" San: \"When you're busy with new projects, remember to take breaks like this.\" \"Noted, Captain. I can see this trip becoming a regular thing.\" \"Agreed! Next time, let's invite the others too; it'll be fun with a bigger group.\" As the day ended, the Canon Five found that Fair Tide offered more than opportunities and alliances: it also gave them space to rest, recover and simply enjoy life together."},
{"n":961,"title":"The Aftereffects (I)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"The day after their visit to the Fountain, the Canon Five began to notice changes, subtle at first, then impossible to ignore. \"I slept so deeply last night... for the first time in so long, I woke up without that heaviness in my body. It's not just rest... I feel clearer, more balanced. Like my body has finally caught up with me.\" \"The old stiffness in my shoulders is gone, and I didn't realise how much it had been slowing me down until now. I feel stronger, with better endurance. It's subtle, but it's already making a difference.\" \"My breathing feels easier, my energy is brighter, and I'm not as quickly fatigued anymore! I've always been in good shape, but this feels like a version of myself that's... more complete.\" \"The old aches from long travels are gone. My body feels lighter, more resilient. It's like all the little wear and tear over the years has been mended at once.\" \"My mind feels sharper, my focus is steadier... and there's a new sense of calm I didn't expect. It's strange... like a weight I've been carrying for years is simply gone.\" \"It's definitely more than just a bath. Whatever the Fountain did, it worked far deeper than we expected. We're healthier, stronger, and... I feel happier, too. Let's keep an eye on the changes over the next few days. There might still be more effects we haven't noticed yet.\" As the sun set over Fair Tide the Canon Five shared a quiet understanding: the restoration had given them more than renewed strength. It had given them space to live, to work, and to look ahead with greater confidence."},
{"n":962,"title":"The Aftereffects (II)","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"Over the next few days the changes from the Fountain became more apparent. Their bodies recovered quickly, injuries faded and a sense of overall renewal settled in. Devon: \"My focus feels sharper than before. I can think for longer without that usual mental fatigue.\" Sky: \"My stamina's completely different! Training feels easier now, and I recover much faster!\" Levi: \"My injuries, old and new, are gone. My body moves more freely than it has in years.\" Sally: \"My head feels clearer, and my energy stays steady throughout the day. It's a lot easier to keep up with my work now.\" Jade: \"It's more than just physical changes... I feel lighter, as if a weight I didn't even realise I was carrying has been lifted. Not a new person, but a more complete version of myself.\" \"I can't believe we all feel the difference so clearly.\" \"It's strange, isn't it? We didn't expect it to work this well.\" \"And we still don't know everything it will lead to. There could be more changes ahead...\" \"...or consequences we haven't noticed yet.\" \"Whatever comes, we'll face it together, just like everything else.\" The Canon Five knew the Fountain had restored more than their health. Yet the full extent of its impact remained a mystery. For now, they chose to focus on the present: healthier, renewed and ready for what lay ahead at Fair Tide and beyond."},
{"n":963,"title":"Life Afterwards","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"In the weeks that followed, the Canon Five settled into life in Fair Tide, the effects of the Fountain continuing to reveal themselves in quiet but meaningful ways. Jade: \"I've noticed my old splitting headaches are gone, and I haven't felt that constant fatigue in a long time. It's not a sudden change, but a steady improvement. My body feels more stable and resilient now.\" Devon: \"The stiffness in my shoulder has eased significantly. It's a relief to feel more mobile again, and I can keep up with training without worry.\" Sky: \"I used to get run down easily after long travel. Now my recovery is much faster, and I feel more energetic overall. It's like my body can handle hard work and long journeys again without constantly hitting a limit.\" Levi: \"The old injuries I've carried for years feel... healed. There's more flexibility, less pain, and I can move freely again. It's not that I've become superhuman, just that my body is finally back to how it should be.\" Sally: \"I'm sleeping better, my focus is clearer, and I no longer feel the nagging discomfort I used to manage all the time.\" The Fountain's restoration is not a blanket transformation. It removes or repairs negative physical effects and underlying health issues that can be restored. It improves overall vitality, recovery and resilience. It does not automatically grant magical abilities. It does not fundamentally change who you are. It does not force any specific future outcomes. Rather than an overnight miracle, the Fountain had given them something more valuable: restoration, relief and a healthier foundation for the lives they hoped to build from here."},
{"n":964,"title":"Two Kinds of Veyren Blood","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"One evening in Fair Tide the Canon Five found a quiet moment to reflect on what they had learned since the Fountain, especially about bloodlines and identity in Veyren. \"It's clearer now... there are actually two kinds of Veyren bloodline in this world.\" \"Right. It helps us understand why some of us are different from the new residents, even after the Fountain.\" \"For us, you and I were already changed by Veyren long before we ever thought of having children. Our bodies, blood and life functions had been fundamentally altered by this world, which means any children we have are Veyren by lineage, not just by environment.\" \"Exactly. Our twins are considered pure-blood Veyren children because they come from two parents who had already been transformed by Veyren itself. They're not Lunareth-born who later adapted to Veyren. Their foundation is already Veyren, from the very beginning of their conception.\" Pure-blood Veyren (e.g. San and Joel's children): born from parents who are already Veyren-transformed; inherit Veyren physiology and adaptation naturally; considered fully Veyren by origin and lineage. Lunareth-born residents (e.g. new arrivals, Fair Tide locals): originally born on Lunareth; remain Lunareth-born even after Fountain restoration; gain restored health, removed ailments and improved vitality, but their core origin remains Lunareth. Sky: \"So the Fountain doesn't change where we were born, or our origin?\" Levi: \"That's right. The Fountain restores and repairs what can be restored, like health, vitality and physical conditions. It returns us to a healthier, more complete state, but it doesn't rewrite our birthplace or make us magical by default.\" Sally: \"In other words, we can all benefit from it, but our fundamental identity, Lunareth-born or Veyren, remains the same as before.\" The Fountain gave them restored health and greater vitality, while Veyren itself defined lineage, origin, and what could be passed on to the next generation."},
{"n":965,"title":"Back to Lunareth","part":2,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide Harbour, then Lunareth","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"After their time in Fair Tide the Canon Five prepared to return to Lunareth, carrying with them new strength, restored health and many unanswered questions. \"It feels strange to be heading home again... like we've stepped into a new chapter without fully knowing what it means yet.\" \"I'm just glad we all made it back in good shape. Whatever the Fountain changed, it's certainly done us a lot of good.\" \"My body feels lighter, my mind clearer, and I have more energy than I've had in years.\" \"I'm curious to see how these changes settle over time. For now I'm just happy to feel this good.\" \"Same here. We can figure out the rest later. For now, let's just enjoy being on our way home.\" A few days later the Canon Five returned to Lunareth. Life in the capital continued as it always had: busy, familiar and full of movement. \"It's good to be back. There's so much we need to catch up on: reports, projects and a few overdue plans.\" \"We'll keep an eye on how we continue to feel in the coming weeks.\" \"And maybe once things settle, we can properly look into what exactly the Fountain changed for us.\" \"One step at a time. For now, let's just return to our routines, catch up with people, and live normally again.\" The Fountain had given them renewed vitality and a clearer sense of well-being, but its full impact remained unknown. For now the Canon Five chose to return to their lives in Lunareth with open minds, cautious curiosity and the quiet understanding that some answers would come in time."},
{"n":966,"title":"Direct Approach","part":3,"loc":"🏝️ Fair Tide and the key route","who":"Jade, Devon, Sky, Levi and Sally","text":"Soon after reuniting in Fair Tide, Jade and her team took on their first joint mission, a perfect showcase of how the Canon Five approach a threat. Jade: \"We start with a full investigation: confirm the source, the routes, and the people involved.\" Devon: \"Then we commit. No half measures once we have proof.\" Sky: \"We make our move directly, cutting off their supply and dealing with the core threat.\" Levi: \"Hold the line, secure the area, and make sure the civilians are protected.\" Sally: \"And we stay until it's resolved. No hit-and-run, no leaving a mess for others to clean up.\" Their findings led them to a black market group harassing traders and villagers along a key route. With the evidence in hand, the Canon Five moved at once. Jade: \"You're safe now. We've cleared the area, and the route will be patrolled for the next few weeks.\" Devon: \"The threat has been neutralised, the stolen goods recovered, and the affected villages reported for further support.\" Sky: \"A direct approach works best when we combine solid information, commitment, and follow-through.\" Levi: \"No unnecessary delays, no allowing the threat to grow, just a clean and complete resolution.\" Sally: \"And most importantly... people get to go back to their daily lives without fear. That is always the point.\" The mission reaffirmed the Canon Five's shared approach: investigate thoroughly, act decisively, hold their ground and protect those caught in the middle. It was a strong start for the new quests ahead."},
{"n":967,"title":"Rapid Response","part":3,"loc":"🌲 A forest rendezvous","who":"Sally and Levi","text":"While the rest of the Canon Five often favour direct engagement and methodical investigation, Sally and Levi operate with a different specialty: rapid response and precision operations. Levi: \"Not every threat needs a full assault. Sometimes the best result comes from speed, stealth and knowing when to strike.\" Sally: \"We move fast, hit where it hurts, get what we need, and get the civilians out safely, before the enemy even realises what happened.\" Sally: \"We reposition here, cut off their escape route, and create a diversion at the front.\" Levi: \"Then we move in, secure the target, extract the civilians, and withdraw before they can regroup. Small team. Silent approach. We move at once.\" Their team struck with speed and precision. A brief, coordinated ambush disrupted the enemy, allowing the civilians to be escorted out while the Canon Five withdrew without prolonging the fight. \"Keep moving. You're safe now. We're getting you out of here.\" \"Clear ahead. Maintain pace, no stops until we're at the rendezvous point.\" Sally: \"That's the advantage of mobility: minimal exposure, maximum result.\" Levi: \"Fast in, fast out. The longer you stay, the more risks you create.\" The mission was another success, a reminder that the Canon Five's strength lay not only in power but in the different skills each member brought to the team. Direct force, careful investigation or rapid response, all served the same goal: protecting people, resolving threats and keeping Fair Tide safe."},
{"n":968,"title":"The Fair Tide Scouts","part":3,"loc":"🌲 The hills above Fair Tide","who":"Levi, Iris and KW Liang","text":"Levi began working more closely with Iris and Liang, the Fair Tide scouts who see the world through different strengths but with the same purpose. \"Same objective, different approach.\" \"Let's show you how the Fair Tide Scouts work.\" \"Observation, movement, positioning... and knowing when to act.\" Iris, Fair Tide Scout: familiar Ash (fox, now a cat after the change in Fair Tide); stealth, tracking and observation. \"The key isn't just finding what's there: it's seeing what others miss.\" KW Liang, Fair Tide Scout: familiar Snowball (rabbit); route finding, terrain awareness and quiet reconnaissance. \"A good route saves time, people, and unnecessary risk.\" Levi: \"Then let's combine them. Iris finds the signs, Liang maps the route, and we decide our move from there.\" Liang: \"The main trail is too exposed. There's a ridge here; it gives cover and a clear view of the target area.\" Iris: \"I've picked up recent tracks: a small group, heavily armed, heading to the supply cache before nightfall.\" \"So we move along the ridge, confirm their numbers, and prep an ambush point.\" By dusk the three put their plan into action, quietly, precisely and in sync: Iris on tracking and surveillance, Liang on route and positioning, Levi on cover and engagement. \"Clean extraction, no civilian casualties, and the supplies secured.\" \"A good start. Different skills really cover each other's blind spots.\" \"This is what Fair Tide scouting is about: information, terrain, people, and acting at the right moment.\" Their first joint operation proved to be a success, a clear reminder that the Fair Tide Scouts function best not as individuals but as a coordinated team."},
{"n":969,"title":"The Lookout","part":3,"loc":"⚓ The Crimson Tide","who":"Senedra and the Crimson Tide crew","text":"From Tribute's point of view, Senedra is not just a scout: she is a bridge between worlds, a member of Crimson Tide's crew and a key part of Fair Tide's community team. Senedra, Crimson Tide crew and Fair Tide member: scout and lookout; paramedic (Brunei); delivery support (Aisyah's orders); Fair Tide medical team (Dr AA and Jovie). \"Different worlds, different duties, but the same people to protect.\" On the Crimson Tide, Senedra is family: a trusted crew member who keeps watch, supports missions and brings real-world experience that strengthens the crew. Senedra's roles, versatile, field-ready and community-focused: shipboard lookout, the crew's main lookout, who watches the horizons, weather, vessels, unusual movement and approaching threats; paramedic (Brunei), a trained paramedic who rides the ambulance, responds to emergencies and brings real-world medical experience; delivery support (side income), who runs delivery routes, often handling and transporting orders for Aisyah's customers; and Fair Tide medical team (Dr AA and Jovie), providing clinical support, triage and community care. \"As the crew's primary lookout, Senedra keeps an eye on what others might miss, long before it becomes a threat. She can join missions when needed, scouting, field support, extraction or medical cover, but her main role remains watching over the crew and the sea. In Fair Tide, Senedra's medical skills and calm judgment are just as valuable, from treating injuries to supporting Dr AA and Jovie in the community.\" To Tribute, Senedra shows that the people of Fair Tide and Crimson Tide don't live in separate worlds: they work, care and watch over each other. A scout, a medic, a lookout, a delivery rider and a friend: practical skills, community care and a shared commitment to keep their people safe."},
{"n":970,"title":"Information Moves Faster","part":3,"loc":"⚓ The Crimson Tide","who":"Levi, Senedra, Iris and KW Liang","text":"Levi began working with the scouts to turn what they find, from horizons to hidden trails, into faster, more precise action for the Crimson Tide. Levi: \"Information is powerful, but only if it leads to action quickly.\" Senedra: \"Each of us sees a different part of the picture.\" Iris: \"Together, we turn that picture into a response.\" KW Liang: \"Faster information. Clearer plans. A crew that moves as one.\" A coordinated network of watch, find, map and respond. Senedra, shipboard lookout: watches horizons and weather, spots approaching threats, tracks vessels and unusual movement, issues early alerts to the crew. Iris, stealth and tracking scout: tracks targets and movement, gathers information discreetly, reconnaissance in sensitive areas, detects signs others might miss. KW Liang, route and terrain scout: maps safe and efficient routes, assesses terrain and travel risks, identifies resources and ambush points, supports long-distance planning. Levi, rapid-response covert specialist: turns scout intel into field action, leads small fast response teams, handles infiltration, interception and threat containment, coordinates with the crew for immediate follow-up. With clear roles in place, the scouts ran a coordinated exercise, from spotted movement to on-ground response. Senedra: \"I spotted a vessel moving unusually close.\" Iris: \"I've tracked its course and speed. It's not a regular trade route.\" KW Liang: \"I can follow it unnoticed and confirm its purpose.\" Levi: \"Good. We'll use the covert route, confirm the cargo, and decide the next move on site.\" 1. Detect (lookout alert). 2. Confirm (tracking and intel). 3. Plan (route and approach). 4. Respond (rapid field action). \"This works: from sighting to action, with no wasted time.\" \"Different skills, same goal. It feels good to see it all come together.\" \"Now the crew can respond faster, safer, and with a clearer picture of what's ahead.\" \"Information moves faster now, and that means more lives protected.\" The Crimson Tide Scout System: a flexible, coordinated network of watch, insight, movement and action, ensuring that no threat reaches the crew unseen, and that everyone in Fair Tide remains safe."},
{"n":971,"title":"Sally and Sairen","part":3,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Sally Sun and Sairen","text":"At Fair Tide, Sally Sun and Sairen began working more closely on intelligence and quickly discovered they shared the same goal, even if their methods were very different. Sally Sun, Information Specialist and Agent: \"People talk. I just know how to listen.\" Sairen, Intelligence Specialist and Network Coordinator: \"Information is useful, when it is organised.\" Sally: \"You'd be surprised what people will share over tea, a drink, or a little flattery.\" Sairen: \"And that's where I come in. What you gather, I sort, verify, and connect to wider patterns: people, locations, movements and risks.\" Sally, social intelligence: builds rapport and trust; gathers news, rumours and insider talk; picks up informal leads; uncovers hidden motives through people. Sairen, organised intelligence: verifies and cross-checks information; builds information networks; compiles structured reports; identifies patterns, risks and next steps. Sally: \"Different methods, but it works well together, doesn't it?\" Sairen: \"It does. You bring the pieces from the people, I arrange them into a clearer picture.\" Sally: \"In the end, it's the same purpose: keeping the crew informed, prepared, and one step ahead.\" Sairen: \"Exactly. Different paths, shared objective.\" With Sally's instinct for people and Sairen's skill in building intelligence networks, the Crimson Tide gained a stronger, more complete flow of information across Fair Tide, from whispers in the market to reports that guide real action. Two different minds, two different methods, but together they turn scattered information into the kind of knowledge that keeps the crew, Fair Tide and their allies safer."},
{"n":972,"title":"Mirelle","part":3,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Mirelle, Sally and Sairen","text":"In Fair Tide, Mirelle quickly proved herself a valuable ally, not through field skills or archives, but through something far more subtle: her keen eye for people, politics and the spaces in between. Mirelle, Queen of Altan and Political and Social Observer: \"People reveal more in casual conversation than in formal reports.\" While others focused on reports, trade routes and hard evidence, Mirelle watched the people: their tone, choices of company, small favours exchanged, and the tensions they tried to hide. Mirelle: \"Did you notice how the merchant shifted topics when the council's expansion was mentioned?\" Sally: \"Mm. He dismissed it lightly, but his aide sent a message immediately after. That's interesting.\" Sairen: \"That detail wasn't in any of the formal reports. Good catch, Mirelle.\" Mirelle: \"People are far more candid in relaxed settings, at banquets, markets, even casual games, than in official meetings.\" Mirelle's observations: subtle shifts in alliances; unspoken rivalries within the council; key figures who appear cooperative, but aren't; emerging interests around Fair Tide's trade expansion; individuals who may become valuable contacts. With her grace, experience and unerring instincts for people, Mirelle became an indispensable part of the Crimson Tide's intelligence efforts in Fair Tide. She saw what others missed, not in records or research, but in the human details that often reveal the bigger truths."},
{"n":973,"title":"Three Ways of Knowing People","part":3,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Sally Sun, Sairen and Mirelle","text":"As they compared notes from their recent findings, the three of them realised that their approaches to information were different: not competing, but complementary. \"Three different perspectives... but together, they give us a clearer picture.\" Sally Sun, social intelligence: \"People tell you a lot, if you know how to listen and make them feel at ease.\" She gathers information through people and conversation, picks up rumours, sentiment and hidden motives, and builds trust and rapport easily. Sairen, organised networks: \"Information only becomes useful when it is verified, organised and placed in the right context.\" He builds and maintains structured information networks, verifies, cross-checks and connects multiple sources, and maps patterns, movements and risks across regions. Mirelle, political and interpersonal observation: \"Politics is more than official records. It is in how people speak, who they stand with, and what they choose not to say.\" She reads people, alliances and unspoken tensions, notices subtle shifts in behaviour, tone and influence, and understands the bigger political picture and its long-term implications. Sally: \"So, I find out what people are saying.\" Sairen: \"I connect and organise it, turning pieces into a clear network.\" Mirelle: \"And I see what it means for the people and the political landscape.\" Three ways of knowing people: through conversation, through networks and through observation. Different strengths, different perspectives, but a shared purpose: information that helps Fair Tide, the Crimson Tide and their allies make better decisions in a changing world."},
{"n":974,"title":"The Message Before the Fight","part":3,"loc":"🌙 A Fair Tide outpost","who":"Sally, Sairen, Mirelle and the crew","text":"A new lead arrived: a message hinting at a covert shipment and a planned attack against a Fair Tide outpost. This time they decided to put their growing system to the test: scouting, information and combat working together as one. Sally: \"The message is real. It's a cover shipment, and we know who's moving it, and why.\" Sairen: \"I've traced the network. Three stops, rotating guards, and a meeting before the attack. We can intercept them here.\" Mirelle: \"And here are the pieces they missed: a recent shift in their allies, internal tension, and a key figure who will be present in person.\" The connected plan. Scout (field): confirm location, route and troop strength. Information (network): verify the message, track contacts and timing. Combat (direct): intercept, neutralise the threat and secure the evidence. Sally, social intelligence: confirms the sender's identity, uncovers their motive, and exposes the real target behind the shipment. Sairen, information networks: maps the route, links their allies, and synchronises updates between the scouts and the combat team. Mirelle, political observation: reads the key players, predicts their moves, and identifies the best point to strike with minimal fallout. 1. Scouting, confirmation: the scouts confirm the shipment, the number of guards and the presence of the key figure. 2. Information, synchronisation: Sairen's network sends real-time updates, route changes, reinforcements and the exact timing of the meeting. 3. Combat, interception: with the information in place the crew moves swiftly, intercepts the target and prevents the attack before it begins. Sally: \"Smooth coordination. The scouts gave us the picture, the network kept it clear, and the fight sealed.\" Sairen: \"No gaps, no guesswork. This is what it looks like when all three systems work as one.\" Mirelle: \"Information finds the truth, observation sees the bigger picture, and action gives it result. That is a system we can rely on, for Fair Tide and beyond.\" Mission result: threat neutralised; key figure captured; network exposed; evidence secured; alliance strengthened; integrated system proven. The mission proved more than just a success: it showed that scouting, information and combat were no longer separate tools, but parts of one connected system that made the Crimson Tide and their allies stronger together."},
{"n":975,"title":"The Medical Circle","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the infirmary","who":"Sky, Jenika, Maera, Eliz, Dr AA, Sister Wren, Senedra and Jovie","text":"With growing movement across Fair Tide and new threats on the horizon, Sky and Jenika brought together the key medical minds from both crews to form a shared Medical Circle, combining healing, care, research and field support. Sky: \"A larger crew, wider routes and greater risks mean we need a medical system that works across both our crews.\" Jenika: \"So today, we're forming the Medical Circle: not just to treat injuries, but to strengthen health, prevent outbreaks, and support longer missions together.\" Maera, Midwife and Maternal Care Lead. Eliz, Cleric and Healing Support. Dr AA, Physician and Medical Specialist. Sister Wren, Healer and Cleric. Senedra, Scout and Field Medic. Jovie, Infirmary Coordinator and Clinical Support. Sky: \"We'll standardise treatment protocols, share medical records, and build a mobile support system for field operations.\" Maera: \"Maternal, long-term and general care will also be included. A healthier crew is a stronger crew.\" Dr AA: \"With both crews working together, we can respond faster, treat more people, and prepare for what comes next. And we'll keep researching, especially on long-term vitality, recovery and the uniqueness of life in Veyren.\" Eliz: \"Healing is more than treating wounds. It's rest, stability, hope, and a crew that looks after one another.\" Senedra: \"I'll work on the field side: preparedness, first response, and support for scouting teams during operations.\" Jovie: \"I'll coordinate supplies, rotations and the infirmary schedule. With a clear system, we can keep everyone mission-ready and cared for.\" From different expertise and experiences the Medical Circle was born, a shared support system for Fair Tide, the Crimson Tide and the journeys ahead: unified medical support, shared protocols and records, field and emergency care, maternal and long-term care, ongoing research and prevention, and crew health and readiness."},
{"n":976,"title":"Different Kinds of Medicine","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the infirmary","who":"Sky, Jenika and the Medical Circle","text":"As the Medical Circle took shape the crew formalised each role. Rather than a single \"healer\" for everything, they built a complete medical team, with different expertise, working together for Veyren's people and travellers alike. Sky: \"Medicine isn't just healing. It covers life at every stage, from birth to growth, illness, injury and recovery.\" Jenika: \"With each of us focusing on our strength, we can give better care, respond faster in emergencies, and support long-term health for Fair Tide and beyond.\" Maera, Veyren OB-GYN and Paediatric Specialist: maternal health and pregnancy care; childbirth and postnatal recovery; infant and child care and development; women's health, reproductive and hormonal. Eliz, Healer (Primary Care): general healing and recovery; injury treatment and wound care; restoration, stamina and condition support; longer-term healing and rehabilitation. Dr AA, Physician (Diagnosis and Treatment): medical diagnosis and treatment plans; management of illnesses, acute and chronic; preventive care and health monitoring; medical guidance for long missions and expeditions. Sister Wren, Veyren Healer and Support Specialist: Veyren-focused healing methods (energy, alignment, recovery); emotional and spiritual support; stamina, resilience and stress recovery; support during major treatments and high-risk missions. Senedra, Paramedic and Emergency Support: first response and field triage; emergency treatment (injuries, acute illness, stabilisation); evacuation and field care during expeditions; emergency preparedness and training. Jovie, Nursing and Clinical Support: patient care and ongoing monitoring; treatment preparation and administration; clinical operations (supplies, schedules, records); care coordination between all medical roles. From new life and growing children, to healing and recovery, to emergencies in the field, diagnosis, treatment and long-term health, and the Veyren-based healing and support that keeps the crew strong, all working together as one medical circle. Different expertise, a shared purpose: not just to treat illness, but to protect life, strengthen resilience and support every journey ahead. Key takeaways: clear roles, distinct expertise; covers life stages and different medical needs; combines conventional and Veyren healing; field, emergency and long-term care; a stronger, more resilient crew and community."},
{"n":977,"title":"Maera's Specialty","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the infirmary","who":"Maera, San, Joel and the Medical Circle","text":"Among the Medical Circle, Maera's expertise stands apart: she is the only one who can properly diagnose and manage Veyren pregnancy, from early confirmation to the child's development and care. Maera: \"Veyren pregnancy is different from human pregnancy. The signs, timing and development follow Veyren's own rhythms. It's something that must be recognised by experience, observation and a deep knowledge of Veyren biology.\" Maera: \"I still remember this day. When I confirmed you were carrying twins, San, it was through the signs of your body, energy and Veyren rhythms. You were one of the happiest diagnoses I've made.\" \"You guided us through every step: the pregnancy, the delivery, and even afterwards, when we were still learning to be parents.\" \"From the delivery to their first check-ups, the twins were always in good hands with you.\" \"And you've continued to look after them through every stage, from their first steps, growing stronger each year.\" Maera: \"Seeing them now, healthy, bright and full of life, that's the best reward for any healer.\" \"You've been more than our doctor, Maera. You've been part of our family.\" Maera: \"That's what I love about Veyren medicine: we don't just help bring life into the world, we also get to see them grow, learn and thrive.\" Maera: \"So when it comes to Veyren pregnancy, whether a first child, twins, or a later pregnancy, I'll be the one to assess, confirm and create the care plan. The rest of the Medical Circle will then support according to the stage and need.\" \"It makes sense. It's a specialised field, and your experience with San and the twins shows exactly why.\" \"We're lucky to have you, Maera. Your expertise brings both skill and heart to the circle.\" More than expertise, Maera brings continuity, from the first confirmation of life, to birth, childhood and beyond: a trusted partner in the long journey of Veyren families. Key takeaways: Maera is the Veyren OB-GYN and paediatric specialist. Only Maera can properly diagnose Veyren pregnancy. She diagnosed San's twin pregnancy and managed their care from pregnancy to childhood. She provides continuity of care across life stages."},
{"n":978,"title":"Something Different","part":3,"loc":"🏡 Jade and Devon's home","who":"Jade and Devon","text":"Days after returning from Fair Tide, Jade began to notice subtle changes in her body: unfamiliar, not quite an illness, but different enough to make her pay attention. Jade: \"...It's strange. I'm more tired than usual... and my appetite has changed too. But it doesn't feel like an illness. Could it be the long travel? Or just my body finally catching up after everything that happened in Fair Tide?\" Devon: \"You've been more tired lately. Your meals are lighter, and you rest more than usual. Are you feeling unwell?\" Jade: \"It's nothing serious, I think. Just... different. Maybe it's still the after-effects from the journey?\" Devon: \"It could be travel fatigue, a change in diet, or your body adjusting to the longer voyage. Let's keep an eye on it for now. If it doesn't settle, we can ask Maera for advice later.\" Jade: \"Hmm... I'm actually craving things I don't usually crave. And certain smells feel much stronger than before... And I've been falling asleep so easily... It's unusual for me.\" Devon (to himself, writing): \"The timing is interesting... but it's too early to draw any conclusion. I'll just make sure she gets enough rest, proper meals and a lighter schedule for now.\" Devon: \"Whatever this is, we'll figure it out together. There's no rush, Jade.\" Jade: \"Mm... I'm not worried. It's just... different. But it feels safe, and... peaceful.\" For now Jade and Devon chose to observe, rest and adjust, not as expectant parents but as partners facing another new change in their journey together. Key takeaways: Jade experiences unfamiliar physical changes after Fair Tide; the symptoms are subtle and not immediately linked to pregnancy; possible causes are travel fatigue, body adjustment or other factors; Jade and Devon choose to monitor and rest first, with Maera's advice as a later step."},
{"n":979,"title":"The Diagnosis","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the Medical Circle","who":"Jade, Devon and Maera","text":"When the changes continued, Jade and Devon finally sought Maera's assessment at the Fair Tide Medical Circle. Maera: \"I've completed my assessment. Jade... you are pregnant.\" Jade: \"I... I'm pregnant...?\" Devon: \"So it's real... We're going to have a child...?\" Maera: \"Yes. It's a healthy pregnancy, for now. You're still in the early stage, which is ideal for rest and proper care.\" Maera: \"There's another important thing to understand. The Fountain of Youth may have restored reproductive function for both of you: function that might have been previously damaged, suppressed, or unable to work normally before. The Fountain doesn't just remove illness or burden from the body. It helps the body return to a more complete and balanced state, including the natural ability to conceive and carry a child.\" Maera: \"This isn't about who could or couldn't have children before. That distinction was never necessary, and it doesn't matter now. What matters is that your bodies are now in a state where new life is possible, and you're expecting one.\" Jade and Devon: \"Thank you, Maera... Truly. We... we'll take good care of both of us.\" The news brings a quiet, profound joy, not just for the new life on the way but for what it means: healing, renewal and a future they can now build together more fully. Key takeaways: Maera confirms that Jade is pregnant; the Fountain may have restored reproductive function that was previously damaged, suppressed or unable to function normally; the story does not identify Jade or Devon as \"the infertile one\"; the focus is on healing, restoration and the new life ahead."},
{"n":980,"title":"Not Quite Either","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the Medical Circle","who":"Jade, Devon, Maera, San, Joel and their twins Vaeren and Joelle","text":"With the pregnancy confirmed, Jade and Devon asked Maera what to expect: whether their child would be like San and Joel's twins. Maera: \"It's natural to wonder if your child will be like San and Joel's twins. The answer is... not exactly.\" Maera: \"San and Joel had already been fundamentally altered by Veyren, in body, vitality and their very life rhythm, long before their twins were conceived. Because of that, their twins are pure-blood Veyren children, fully aligned with Veyren's biology, growth and development.\" The twins are Vaeren and Joelle. Jade: \"But we're still Lunareth-born... So our child will be different from the twins?\" Maera: \"Yes. You and Devon have not undergone the same degree of Veyren transformation as San and Joel. So your child will most likely be a Veyren-Lunareth hybrid. They may inherit some Veyren traits, such as resilience, vitality or adaptation, while still carrying their Lunareth roots.\" Maera: \"The exact mix will be unique to your child: not a lesser version of either world, but their own balance of both. In short, not quite Veyren, not quite Lunareth, but a bridge between the two.\" The news brings a deeper sense of meaning: their child will be a link between worlds, carrying both heritage and possibility into the future. Key takeaways: San and Joel had already been fundamentally altered by Veyren; their twins, Vaeren and Joelle, are pure-blood Veyren children; Jade and Devon remain Lunareth-born; their child will most likely be a Veyren-Lunareth hybrid, expected to carry a unique balance of both worlds' traits."},
{"n":981,"title":"An Old Bloodline, A New World","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the Medical Circle","who":"Jade, Devon and Maera","text":"With the nature of the pregnancy understood, Jade and Devon now considered what it might mean for their child: not in terms of power, but in terms of heritage, origin and the world they would grow up in. Devon: \"So our child will carry parts of both our heritage... And also be shaped by Veyren's influence?\" Jade: \"Yes... a blend of our bloodlines and the world we're living in now.\" Maera: \"Your child draws from three important sources. Jade, you carry the Gold lineage, the legacy that reaches back to Dima-Xima. Devon, your blood is of House Xuanji, the Dragonvale lineage, known for its resilience, adaptability and deep roots. And now, with life developing within Veyren, this child will also be shaped by Veyren's environment and its unique influence on growth and development.\" Jade: \"That's a lot to take in... But it feels right. A child born from both of us, from our histories, our homes, and the life we're building in Veyren.\" Devon: \"Regardless of all that, our hope is simple: for them to be healthy, kind, and able to choose their own path.\" Maera: \"Exactly. This heritage gives them a unique foundation, but it doesn't define their fate. They aren't a chosen one, nor are they automatically overpowered.\" Maera: \"Children of mixed heritage can have a wider range of potential, in health, resilience, adaptation, and how they connect with both worlds. But like any child, they will also have their own personality, strengths, and challenges. They will grow in their own time, in their own way.\" It isn't a story of destiny or supreme power, but of convergence: of old bloodlines, new influences, and a life that belongs to the next generation. Key takeaways: the child carries three influences (Jade's Gold / Dima-Xima heritage, Devon's House Xuanji / Dragonvale bloodline, and Veyren's developmental influence); this does not make the child automatically overpowered or prophetic; the child may have a wider range of potential (health, resilience, adaptation); their growth, personality and path will be their own, unfolding naturally in time."},
{"n":982,"title":"The Future Jade Never Expected","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the Medical Circle","who":"Jade, Devon and Maera","text":"With the nature of the pregnancy understood, Jade and Devon took time to consider what it truly meant. Maera: \"This is not a reward. And it is not destiny choosing for you. It is the return of possibility: a future your bodies can now hold.\" Jade: \"So this child isn't proof that we were promised something?\" Devon: \"No prophecy. No debt. Just a life we may choose to welcome.\" Maera: \"Exactly. Healing reopened what was closed. What you build from here is still yours.\" Jade: \"Then maybe that's why it feels so precious. Not because fate owed it to us...\" Devon: \"...but because it was never something to take for granted.\" Not a destiny assigned from above, but a possibility returned through healing, choice and time. Jade: \"A future I never expected.\" Devon: \"A future we can still choose, together.\" Maera: \"That is enough. Let it be hope, not burden.\" What lay ahead was not a reward, nor a path written for them in advance: it was simply a future made possible again, one they would meet with gratitude, choice and love."},
{"n":983,"title":"Apparently Two Was Not Enough","part":3,"loc":"🩺 Fair Tide: the Medical Circle","who":"Sally, Levi and Maera","text":"Lately Sally had been feeling different: foods she once loved now made her turn away, while strange cravings appeared at the most unexpected times. Sally: \"This is getting strange... I can't stomach it at all today... But now I suddenly want something sweet...? Levi... I think we should check with Maera.\" Levi: \"Hmm? Something wrong? You've been more picky with food lately...\" After listening to Sally's recent symptoms, her changing appetite, heightened sensitivity and other subtle signs, Maera gave them a thoughtful look and her answer was clear. Sally: \"So... it's confirmed?\" Maera: \"Yes... Sally, you're pregnant again.\" Levi: \"...Again? Not another one.\" Sally (laughing): \"You say that as if the first two weren't already a handful. I'm surprised you're not used to it by now.\" Levi: \"Two was already plenty... We were just starting to have a little more time to breathe.\" Sally: \"Still... this is a blessing, Levi. Unexpected perhaps... but a welcome one.\" Levi: \"...You're right. It may not have been the timing we planned... But it's still our child.\" So, with a mixture of exasperation, laughter and quiet acceptance, Sally and Levi prepared once more for the next little life that had already chosen them."},
{"n":984,"title":"The Family Network","part":3,"loc":"🏯 Tribute: the Stanson family","who":"Sally, Levi, Lenny and their children","text":"As news of Sally's pregnancy spread within their family there was no worry for their older children. The two remained well cared for, surrounded by people who loved them, guided them and kept them thriving. Lenny: \"The children will always have a home with me, no matter what. As their godfather, that hasn't changed: if anything, my role in their lives only grows stronger.\" Sally: \"It's such a relief knowing they're surrounded by family... And that you're still there for them, Lenny.\" Lenny: \"Always. They are family, not just yours and Levi's, but all of ours.\" Levi: \"Knowing they're in good hands lets us focus on what comes next.\" With Lenny's steady support and the wider family network around them the children continued to learn, explore and grow in a nurturing environment. As the family prepared for the arrival of a new life they did so with confidence, knowing that love, care and support extended far beyond their immediate household: a child on the way would change their lives again, but they would face it together, with family by their side."},
{"n":985,"title":"Still Moving","part":3,"loc":"⚓ Fair Tide","who":"Sally, Levi, Lenny and their children","text":"Even with another child on the way, Sally and Levi did not step away from the work they had long committed to: rapid response, crisis support and field operations. Sally: \"Pregnant or not... I'm still Sally.\" Levi: \"And I'm still Levi. We may move a little smarter now, but we're not putting everything on hold.\" They continued to assess threats, coordinate responses and support Fair Tide and its allies, proving that family and duty could coexist with balance and care. Their ability to remain active was possible because they were not doing it alone. With Lenny as their godfather and a strong network of family and trusted allies, their children were well cared for, supported and never left behind. Levi: \"Knowing our family is in good hands... I can focus on what needs to be done without worry.\" Sally: \"And that's what makes this different. We're not choosing between family and the life we built...\" Levi: \"...because we have both.\" Life had grown busier, more complex and a little more chaotic, but for Sally and Levi that was exactly how they liked it: still on the move, still in the field, and still building a future for their family, together."},
{"n":986,"title":"The Research Results","part":3,"loc":"📚 Fair Tide: the research hall","who":"Fen, Adrian, Renn, Erynn and Mimi","text":"At Fair Tide's research hall Fen, Adrian, Renn, Erynn and Mimi presented the results of their long study into the Black Pearl. \"Our research confirms that the Black Pearl predates Dragonvale's current dynasty.\" \"Its primary nature is restoration and preservation: not just healing, but the renewal and continued stability of life, land and systems.\" \"The Pearl is compatible with multiple ancient systems, including Dragonvale, Lunareth and others we've identified.\" \"It is also capable of functioning outside Lunareth. It does not require a permanent link to Lunareth to remain operational.\" \"Most importantly, the restoration network we established is now self-sustaining. The Pearl does not need to remain inside Lunareth any longer.\" \"As for its ultimate original owner, our findings are clear on one point: it remains unknown.\" Key findings: older than Dragonvale's current dynasty; connected to restoration and preservation; compatible with multiple ancient systems; capable of functioning outside Lunareth; not required to remain in Lunareth (the restoration network is now self-sustaining); ultimate original owner: unknown."},
{"n":987,"title":"Custodians","part":3,"loc":"📚 Fair Tide: the research hall","who":"Jade, Devon, Adrian, Fen, Renn, Erynn, Mimi, San and Joel","text":"With the research results in hand, Jade and Devon began considering whether Devon should remain the sole long-term custodian of the Black Pearl. Jade: \"Historically, Devon has carried the responsibility alone.\" Devon: \"But now that we know more about the Pearl... it may be time to reconsider whether I should remain the sole long-term custodian.\" \"San and Joel are strong candidates. They have survived more than a decade without ordinary aging. They also have access to inter-world travel, the Horizon Engine, and permanent access to multiple worlds. They have consistently demonstrated their trustworthiness in every world they have worked in.\" Jade: \"So this is not about removing you from the role, Devon. It's about building a stronger, more resilient custodianship, one that can protect the Pearl across worlds and for the long term.\" \"As for the research team, we are aligned that Adrian and Fen are the more suitable experts to take on a larger role in the ongoing Pearl research and network management.\" Not a replacement, but an expansion of custodianship. Devon remains the current custodian. San and Joel are proposed as co-custodians. Adrian and Fen take on a larger role in the ongoing Pearl research and network management. Purpose: stronger protection, continuity and long-term stability across multiple worlds."},
{"n":988,"title":"The Handoff","part":3,"loc":"📚 Fair Tide: the research hall","who":"Jade, Devon, San, Joel and the research team","text":"After careful discussion with the research team Jade and Devon made their decision, entrusting the Black Pearl to San and Joel as its custodians and safekeepers. Jade: \"We entrust the Black Pearl to you, San and Joel.\" Devon: \"From this day forward, you will serve as its custodians and safekeepers.\" San: \"We accept the responsibility. We will safeguard the Pearl, its research, and its legacy, across worlds and for the long term.\" Joel: \"We understand this is a trust, not ownership. We will uphold its purpose and ensure it remains protected and usable for future generations.\" Devon: \"My connection to the Pearl remains, spiritually and historically. It is part of my lineage, and that bond will never truly be severed.\" Jade: \"And Lunareth's restoration network will continue to function as it is now: its operations do not depend on the Pearl's physical presence.\" Devon: \"This is a handoff of responsibility, so the research can continue, expand, and reach further across worlds than any of us could alone.\" Key points: the Black Pearl is entrusted to San and Joel as custodians and safekeepers; they are not the owners of the Pearl; Devon remains spiritually and historically connected to the Pearl; Lunareth's restoration network continues to operate and expand without requiring the Pearl's physical presence."},
{"n":989,"title":"Lunareth","part":3,"loc":"🌐 Fair Tide: the research hall","who":"Jade, Devon, San, Joel and the research team","text":"With the handoff complete the research team turned to the next chapter: Lunareth and its place within the inter-world system. San: \"Lunareth is no longer just a theory or a distant concept. For Crimson Tide, it is now an established destination within our Inter-World Locations system.\" Joel: \"That means we can access Lunareth again, not as a one-time incident, but as a recurring destination.\" \"Through Lunareth, we can travel to multiple worlds, including Tribute, Dragonvale, Altan, Lingering Vale, the Sunken Kingdom, ancient restoration sites, and future regions that will be unlocked in time.\" \"It also creates a permanent research and restoration route, linking these worlds through the Pearl's network, so we can continue our work across realms whenever it is needed.\" \"The Pearl gives you both a lasting reason to return: to monitor its stability, support the restoration network, and ensure the balance between worlds.\" \"Lunareth also provides a central archive and transit hub: a place to exchange knowledge, share research results, and coordinate restoration efforts across destinations.\" \"In short, Lunareth gives the Crimson Tide both access and purpose: a home base for ongoing research, restoration, and future expeditions.\" \"Whether it's to continue the restoration, follow a new lead, or answer a call for help from another world, we will return to Lunareth again and again. It is not just a destination but a lasting bridge: for the Pearl, for the worlds we've come to know, and for what still lies ahead.\""},
{"n":990,"title":"Two Stories Continue","part":3,"loc":"🌅 Fair Tide, at dusk","who":"Jade, Devon, San and Joel","text":"The crossover reached its conclusion, not as an ending but as a new beginning for both Tribute and Crimson Tide. \"Our time together here may be ending, but it is not a farewell. It is a bridge: between our stories, our worlds, and the journeys still to come.\" For Tribute: Crimson Tide becomes part of the existing Ally Network. Jade can access Veyren only through Crimson Tide and its routes. For Crimson Tide: Lunareth becomes another inter-world destination. The Black Pearl expands San and Joel's future beyond Veyren. \"Jade and Devon gain a second home, a place they can return to, build upon, and visit often without abandoning Lunareth.\" \"And San and Joel gain another world, its people, its history, and its unresolved mysteries, that can become future adventures.\" \"The crossover is not the end of Tribute or Crimson Tide. It is the point where both stories become expandable beyond their original borders.\" Key takeaways: the crossover does not close either series; Tribute: Crimson Tide becomes part of the existing Ally Network; Jade can access Veyren only through Crimson Tide and its routes; Crimson Tide: Lunareth becomes another inter-world destination; the Black Pearl expands San and Joel's future beyond Veyren; Jade and Devon gain a second home without abandoning Lunareth; San and Joel gain another world, its people, history and unresolved mysteries for future adventures."}];
